[2026-02-04T17:38:16.785Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011K9G8UfVNyCUx6pLsWarsE","type":"tool_result","content":"# ICE Detention and Deportation Statistics\n\n## Detention Population Growth\n\nThe document reports that **more than 290,000 people have been detained by ICE** since Trump's second term began through mid-October 2025, representing \"a 19 percent increase compared to the same period\" the previous year. As of December 13, 2025, approximately **68,442 people were held in ICE detention**.\n\nThe document does not mention a 75% increase in detention figures.\n\n## Deportation Ratios\n\nThe article does not provide specific deportation ratio data or references to a 1:2 to 14:1 ratio change.\n\n## Denaturalization Efforts\n\nRegarding citizenship revocation, the administration \"planned to denaturalize certain U.S. citizens\" and established \"a quota of up to 200 people per month in 2026.\" The document also notes efforts to \"eliminate constitutionally protected birthright citizenship\" and states the administration \"sought to eliminate funding\" for immigrant legal services.\n\n## Additional Enforcement Metrics\n\nThe administration reportedly set \"a quota...for the number of immigrants to arrest per day\" at **3,000 individuals**, and allocated **$170 billion** toward enforcement and detention infrastructure under the One Big Beautiful Bill Act."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffdb2836-5730-4184-8318-1c286009c5ec","uuid":"28836293-21ad-4c86-87c2-a12d2bec40c1","tool_use_result":{"bytes":106711,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# ICE Detention and Deportation Statistics\n\n## Detention Population Growth\n\nThe document reports that **more than 290,000 people have been detained by ICE** since Trump's second term began through mid-October 2025, representing \"a 19 percent increase compared to the same period\" the previous year. As of December 13, 2025, approximately **68,442 people were held in ICE detention**.\n\nThe document does not mention a 75% increase in detention figures.\n\n## Deportation Ratios\n\nThe article does not provide specific deportation ratio data or references to a 1:2 to 14:1 ratio change.\n\n## Denaturalization Efforts\n\nRegarding citizenship revocation, the administration \"planned to denaturalize certain U.S. citizens\" and established \"a quota of up to 200 people per month in 2026.\" The document also notes efforts to \"eliminate constitutionally protected birthright citizenship\" and states the administration \"sought to eliminate funding\" for immigrant legal services.\n\n## Additional Enforcement Metrics\n\nThe administration reportedly set \"a quota...for the number of immigrants to arrest per day\" at **3,000 individuals**, and allocated **$170 billion** toward enforcement and detention infrastructure under the One Big Beautiful Bill Act.","durationMs":5313,"url":"https://www.vera.org/explainers/weaponizing-the-system-one-year-of-trumps-attacks-on-due-process"}}
